445	### AD-15: Only named, licence-clean, aligned libraries and models ship
446	
447	- **Binds:** NFR-5, NFR-10, NFR-11, FR-103
448	- **Prevents:** an analytics, crash, ads or network SDK arriving directly or transitively; GPL, non-commercial or research-only components; a native library blocking Play upload; the install growing past budget.
449	- **Rule:**
450	  - **The allowlist.** The build fails on any artifact, transitive ones included, that the allowlist doesn't name (ACR-C).
451	  - **Allowed:**
452	    - Google Play Billing with its named Google transitive artifacts, and Play Age Signals;
453	    - AndroidX, including Compose, Room, WorkManager, Navigation 3, Media3 and CameraX;
454	    - the Kotlin standard library, kotlinx.coroutines and kotlinx.serialization;
455	    - on-device runtimes without network code:
456	      - LiteRT-LM, with its GPU accelerator library and its gson and kotlin-reflect dependencies;
457	      - LiteRT;
458	      - our vendored sherpa-onnx build with its ONNX Runtime;
459	      - SQLCipher;
460	      - Rive with ReLinker. Rive's Volley is excluded, and its URL loading is never used.
461	  - **No third-party HTTP client.**
462	  - **Adding an entry** requires a merged-manifest check and a network-code check.
463	  - **Licences.** Allowlist entries and the model and voice manifests carry a licence field. GPL, non-commercial and research-only entries fail the build, and the in-app notices are generated from these fields.
464	  - **Native libraries.** Every `.so` passes a 16 KB ELF alignment check. Vendored native builds use NDK r28 or later.
465	  - **Size gate.** CI fails when the arm64 install size, or any asset class, exceeds its budget line (ACR-D). Until ACR-D is decided, each line is its measured baseline, with both narrator voices included (UX-D). That no-growth comparator is a temporary regression check, not evidence of compliance with NFR-5's 150 MB. `[CONDITIONAL: ACR-D — A-9 and OQ-12 report the three columns with every asset included, and the product owner decides any budget change; fallback: no growth over the measured baseline; NFR-5's 150 MB stays the product target; the demos stay video]`
